// The face of a map board: whatever the render target is showing.
//
// `$rendertarget` IS THE ENGINE'S OWN REFERENCE, not a filename. The material
// system resolves it against whichever RTTextureWidget most recently called
// SetRenderTarget(entity) on this object -- see MCF_Map_BoardComponent, and
// the engine's own comment on RTTextureWidget.SetRenderTarget which says it
// in as many words.
//
// EMISSIVE, AND FULLY SO. A map on a wall in an unlit command post has to
// stay readable, and this surface is showing a screen's worth of pixels
// rather than reflecting a room. Roughness is high and metalness nil so the
// panel does not catch highlights across the middle of the terrain.
MatPBRBasic {
 Color 1 1 1 1
 RoughnessScale 1
 MetalnessScale 0
 Emissive 1 1 1 1
 BCRMap "$rendertarget"
}
